  options,
}
```

I need to add code after this loop that synchronizes alias names. The fix should:

1. For each option, check if the primary name has a value in options
2. If yes, copy that value to all alias names

But there's a subtlety: we only want to copy if the value was actually parsed (not the default). Actually, looking at the default setting code:

```javascript
for (const cliOption of cliOptions) {
  if (!ignoreDefault && cliOption.config.default !== undefined) {
    for (const name of cliOption.names) {
      options[name] = cliOption.config.default
    }
  }
}
```

This sets defaults for ALL names. So if the option wasn't parsed, all names have the default (correct behavior). If the option WAS parsed, only the primary name gets updated, leaving aliases with stale defaults.

